            <ArticleTitle>Follicular carcinoma of thyroid presenting as back pain leading to a delay in diagnosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>334-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The case is described of a 53-year-old man presenting with right-sided low back and thigh pain. Non-urgent investigations showed a metastatic lesion in his right hemipelvis arising from a thyroid primary.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
